   "analysis": "BlockManager.fast_xs has a single-block fast path that returns a view of the block's values for the row, sharing the block's refs. When the columns were first selected with a take, the single block is a temporary copy, so the row Series keeps that whole array alive. Selecting the row first and then the columns avoids this because the row is built from the DataFrame's own data. The fix probably belongs in this path: copy the row when the block is not referenced elsewhere, or otherwise avoid the view.",
